    "physical_description": "Sarong of cotton batik. The cotton is waxed with the tjanting and copper blocks, and dyed indigo, brown and red on a cream ground. The field is patterned with large stylised flowering leafy branches, repeated horizontally, with a butterfly at one end of each row. The head (kepala) and borders are patterned with stylised animals, birds, insects and plants. ",
